      "writtenOn": "2022-09-15T18:12:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sleeping for 10ms sounds expensive for unit tests if we want to do this often. \n\nIs there a way that this can be done synchronously?\n\ne.g. could we monitor the fd_ for incoming streaming and fulfill a std::promise when the incoming string matches our expectation so that we can exit this wait state faster?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "9751586a528090ea5713b9c2bfa4b4b4b611974d",
